{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"logs":["agent chat completed"],"result":"Done. pyknotid 0.5.3 builds from source and is installed into the global Python 3.13 environment with numpy 2.3.0.\n\n## What I did\n\n**Build prerequisites that were missing:** `Cython 3.3.0` and `setuptools 84` (no setuptools at all in the global env), plus runtime deps `networkx, planarity, peewee, vispy, sympy, appdirs, requests, tqdm` and `pytest`.\n\n**Installed with:** `pip install --no-build-isolation .` from `/app/pyknotid`, so the Cython extensions are compiled against your numpy 2.3.0 headers. All four `.so` files are in `site-packages/pyknotid/`: `chelpers`, `ccomplexity` (spacecurves), `cinvariants`, `coctree` (simplify).\n\n## Fixes needed\n\n| Area | Problem | Fix |\n|---|---|---|\n| `setup.py` | `from distutils.extension import Extension`, distutils removed in Py3.12 | `setuptools.extension`; also fixed `install_requires=[...],` (trailing comma made it a tuple) |\n| `chelpers.pyx`, `ccomplexity.pyx`, `cinvariants.pyx` | `np.int` in pyx files, plus Cython 3 needed | compiled unchanged; `ccomplexity` uses `np.int64` for its `long[:]` buffers |\n| numpy aliases removed in 2.0 (`np.float`, `np.int`, `np.bool`, `np.complex`, `np.long`) | 9 modules, ~29 sites | `float64` / `int64` / `bool_` / builtin `complex` |\n| `make/torus.py` | `from fractions import gcd` (gone since Py3.9) | `from math import gcd`; also `divisions` was a numpy float passed as `num` to `linspace`, which numpy 2 rejects (`operator.index`) → wrapped in `int()` |\n| `make/periodic_knot.py` | `n.linspace(..., 30.)` float count | `30` |\n| `spacecurves/periodic.py` | Python-2 implicit relative import `from periodiccell import ...` | package-absolute import; the module now works and `chelpers.find_crossings` runs through it |\n| `representations/representation.py` | planarity 1.0 renamed `networkx_graph` attributes (`pos/start/end` → `vertex_*`/`edge_*`) | normalize back to the old names, works with either version |\n\nOnly `setup.py` and 13 source files changed (57 insertions, 38 deletions); package layout untouched.\n\n## Verification\n\n- Your README snippet runs from a neutral cwd against the installed package: `alexander_polynomial(-1)` → `6.999999999999998`.\n- `pytest tests/ --ignore=tests/test_random_curves.py --ignore=tests/test_catalogue.py` → **18 passed**.\n- Extensions exercised in their original contexts and matching the pure-Python fallbacks: `chelpers.find_crossings` == `helpers.find_crossings`; `ccomplexity.cython_second_order_writhes` / `cython_higher_order_writhe` via `complexity.*`; `cinvariants.vassiliev_degree_3` == python fallback. `coctree` imports too.\n- Spot checks beyond the tests: `mk.torus_knot(7,4).determinant()` → 7, `PeriodicKnot` crossing/gauss-code path, `alexander_polynomial(1j)`, link/octree/smooth paths.\n\n## Left alone (outside your stated scope)\n\n- `tests/test_random_curves.py`: imports `pyknotid.make.randomwalks.quaternionic`, which doesn't exist in this release (dead code, collection error).\n- `tests/test_catalogue.py`: needs the knot catalogue database and `peewee` DB file, not downloaded.\n- `pyknotid/spacecurves/periodicline.py`: upstream stub with a syntax error (`class PeriodicKnot` with no colon); nothing imports it.\n- `pyknotid/catalogue/build.py` needs the optional `rdflib`.\n\nOne note for future rebuilds: use `--no-build-isolation`, otherwise pip builds against a downloaded numpy rather than your 2.3.0."}}
